\pard\f2\b\fs28\fi-1020\li1200\fc0\cf0 Class Description \

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\f0\b0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 NSImageRep is a semi-abstract superclass (ªsemi,º because it has some instance variables and implementation of its own); each of its subclasses knows how to draw an image from a particular kind of source data. While an NSImageRep subclass can be used directly, it's typically used through an NSImage object. An NSImage manages a group of representations, choosing the best one for the current output device.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 There are four subclasses defined in the Application Kit:\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx6740\tx9540\f2\b\fs28\li1900\fc0\cf0 Subclass	Source Data\

\fs6 \

\pard\tx6740\tx9520\f0\b0\fs28\fi-4840\li6740\fc0\cf0 NSBitmapImageRep	Tag Image File Format (TIFF), Windows bitmap (BMP) and other bitmap data\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSCachedImageRep	A rendered image, usually in an off-screen window\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSCustomImageRep	A delegated method that can draw the image\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSEPSImageRep	Encapsulated PostScript code (EPS)\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 You can define other NSImageRep subclasses for objects that render images from other types of source information. New subclasses must be added to the NSImageRep class registry by invoking the 
\b registerImageRepClass:
\b0  class method. The NSImageRep subclass informs the registry of the data types it can support through its 
\b imageUnfilteredFileTypes
\b0 , 
\b imageUnfilteredPasteboardTypes
\b0 , and 
\b canInitWithData:
\b0  class methods. Once an NSImageRep subclass is registered, an instance of that subclass is created any time NSImage encounters the type of data handled by that subclass.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 Subclasses which deal with file and pasteboard types should implement 
\b imageUnfilteredFileTypes
\b0 , 
\b imageUnfilteredPasteboardTypes
\b0 , 
\b initWithData:
\b0 , 
\b canInitWithData:
\b0 , and, if they have the ability to read multiple images from a file, 
\b imageRepsWithData:
\b0 . These last three should not do any filtering; all filtering is automatic.\

\fs14 \

